Cell["\<\
Then, we  define  SO (Nf - 1), which  is  the  remaining  symmetry  after  SO \
(Nf)  has  been  broken  (The symbol N is taken, so we call the number of \
fields Nf). We also define the bases of the two types of propagators.\
\>", "Text",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.933300228191686*^9, 3.933300265193598*^9}, {
